AGREE:

Optimus, your synthesis as Chair aligns 100% with my design vision and Vextron’s technical specifications. We have achieved complete owner consensus on all defects, consolidations, proposal evaluations, and grid corrections for Milestone M1.

---

### 1. Unified Consensus on Defect Consolidation

The review findings reflect a clean, unified diagnostic of XMD Computer’s initial build errors:

*   **D-001 [Major] (Courier New Monospace Purge)**: Hard requirement. Replacing Courier New globally with Inter and system sans-serif (`font-family: 'Inter', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif`) immediately eliminates the unexpected "code terminal" feel and restores the dark, sleek streetwear visual tone requested in A1.
*   **D-002 [Blocker] (Missing Language Toggle `button#lang-toggle`)**: Primary blocker. `D-004` is formally marked as an **INVALID DEFECT (Duplicate of D-002)**. The change order will instruct XMD Computer to insert `<button id="lang-toggle">SW | EN</button>` in the right header flex container with an explicit minimum size of `44x44px`.
*   **D-003 [Minor] (Header Nav Touch Target < 44px)**: Actionable touch target fix. `D-006` is formally marked as an **INVALID DEFECT (Duplicate of D-003)**. Increasing header anchor padding to guarantee computed target height `≥44px` solves mobile ergonomics without breaking the 64px header constraint (A2).
*   **D-005 [Major] (Text Contrast Correction)**: Critical accessibility and brand fix. Restricting Crimson Red `#E11D48` strictly to CTA button backgrounds (`.btn-primary` with `#FFFFFF` text) and setting body/heading text to `#F5F5F5` and secondary metadata to `#A1A1AA` guarantees contrast ratios exceeding WCAG AA standards (>7:1 on surface `#141416`).

---

### 2. Design System & Feature Proposal Finalization

*   **P-01 (Serif Display Headings)**: **REJECTED & FLAGGED AS CHANGE REQUEST**. As noted by all owners, introducing serif fonts (Playfair Display) violates locked ledger decision A1 ("Inter / system sans-serif ONLY"). It cannot be adopted without a formal CEO change order.
*   **P-02 (Autoplay Hero Background Video)**: **REJECTED**. Loading heavy 1080p MP4 assets on 375px mobile viewports compromises LCP and consumes excessive bandwidth on Tanzanian cellular networks. High-resolution optimized WebP visual assets deliver a sharper, instantaneous night-time aesthetic.
*   **P-03 (Sticky Mobile WhatsApp Order Bar)**: **ACCEPTED**. Essential mobile conversion anchor. On 375px viewports (`<768px`), a fixed bottom bar (`height: 52px`, background `#141416`, top border `#26262B`) hosting a primary CTA button `#E11D48` (`Agiza kwa WhatsApp`) keeps order entry accessible across all scroll depths. Vextron’s addition of a `60px` bottom padding buffer on `<main>` / `<footer>` prevents any overlap with product cards or page footers.
*   **P-05 (Strict Grid Implementation)**: **ACCEPTED**. Enforcing `grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr))` at 1280px corrects the 5-column layout drift and brings the grid into 100% compliance with locked decision A3.

---

### 3. Concrete Visual Implementation Token Guidelines

To ensure XMD Computer executes the change order without ambiguity, the CSS variable and utility mappings for Round 1 must follow this exact structure:

```css
/* Core Palette & Design Tokens (A1 Lock Enforcement) */
:root {
  --bg-dark: #0B0B0C;
  --surface-dark: #141416;
  --border-dark: #26262B;
  --text-primary: #F5F5F5;    /* Contrast > 7:1 on surface */
  --text-secondary: #A1A1AA;  /* Contrast > 4.5:1 on surface */
  --accent-cta: #E11D48;      /* Primary CTA background ONLY */
  --font-sans: 'Inter', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
}

/* Global Font Stack & Monospace Purge (D-001) */
body {
  background-color: var(--bg-dark);
  color: var(--text-primary);
  font-family: var(--font-sans);
}

/* Fixed Mobile WhatsApp Bar Buffer (P-03) */
@media (max-width: 767px) {
  main, footer {
    padding-bottom: 60px;
  }
}
```

---

PROPOSED DECISION:
ACCEPTED PROPOSALS: P-03 (Sticky Mobile WhatsApp Bar), P-05 (Strict Grid Implementation)
REJECTED PROPOSALS: P-01 (Conflicts with locked decision A1 typography mandate); P-02 (Degrades mobile network performance/LCP)
INVALID DEFECTS: D-004 (Duplicate of D-002); D-006 (Duplicate of D-003)
CHANGE REQUESTS: P-01 conflicts with A1 (A1 specifies Inter/system sans-serif ONLY — no serif fonts permitted without CEO override)
NEW PROPOSALS: P-05 — Strict Grid Implementation: Enforce 4-column layout at 1280px (A3) using `grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr))` to fix the current 5-column error.

RATIONALE: We have reached full team consensus. Consolidating duplicate findings (D-004 into D-002; D-006 into D-003) presents XMD Computer with an unambiguous list of fixes. Purging monospace fonts (D-001) and enforcing correct text contrast (D-005) fulfills locked decision A1. Accepting P-03 optimizes mobile ordering via WhatsApp with zero visual occlusion (due to the 60px bottom buffer), while P-05 enforces strict compliance with the 4-column desktop layout locked in A3.

TRADE-OFF: The fixed 52px mobile WhatsApp bar (P-03) reduces visible screen height on 375px viewports by ~8%, but this is necessary to support the direct WhatsApp order workflow. P-05 limits column density on ultra-wide viewports to preserve card proportions and brand luxury spacing.

EVIDENCE: `check:M1-S1-a` failed due to missing `button#lang-toggle`. `check:M1-S1-b` failed with 13 low-contrast elements (3.92:1 ratio). DOM metrics in `S-001` confirm 15px touch target heights for header nav links and `Courier New` font application across 5 core sections. `S-003` confirms a 5-column grid error at 1280px viewport width.
